  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member inserting a GIF, I want the GIF search field to stand out clearly from the grid, so that I can see at a glance where to type my search.\n\n### Observed (operator, device, 2026-11-12)\n- In the composer's GIF panel, the search bar is not visible enough: too transparent over the GIF grid.\n\n### Cause (from the code)\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Composer/Gif/GifPickerView.swift:22`: the bar is a `.safeAreaBar(edge: .bottom)` without fill (LOT-185 rule, comment `:5-6`), so the animated, colourful GIFs scroll right under it.\n- `:111-131`: the field's only background is `.quaternary` in a 10 pt rounded rect, a very light fill that the GIFs show through.\n\n### Expected\nA search field that reads as a field over any GIF content, light and dark: e.g. the system search field look (`.searchable` or the iOS 27 glass search field) or an opaque/regular-material capsule, while the grid still runs under the bar (LOT-185). The exact style is to be chosen in the PR with before/after screenshots.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- iPhone and iPad (iOS 27), light and dark, over trending results: the field and its placeholder « Rechercher un GIF… » are clearly visible; contrast of the placeholder meets the HIG minimum.\n- Same behaviour as today: submit searches, ✕ clears, disabled while `phase == .idle`, VoiceOver labels unchanged.\n- Screenshots before/after on the PR; a snapshot or style test if the change is in a testable rule.\n- Related: LOT-098 (GIF panel), LOT-185 (bars), #854 (composer chrome feedback of the same day).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
